From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:19:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: ACPI: processor_idle: Add FFH hierarchy
 coordination hooks

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

Hierarchical Low Power Idle coordination needs architecture-specific help
to identify the direct WFI state, validate and prepare composed firmware
states, and switch the firmware coordination mode. Keep those details
outside the generic ACPI processor-idle code.

Add weak generic hooks that report no hierarchy support. On arm64, identify
the architectural WFI sentinel, check for PSCI OSI support, switch PSCI
coordination mode, and validate the composed power state before entry.

Arm LPI architecture flags state whether core context is lost, while the
PSCI power-state encoding carries the same distinction in StateType. Make
the PSCI context-loss test available to the arm64 ACPI idle code and reject
non-WFI states when these descriptions disagree. Check both the parsed base
state used for direct entry and the final OSI state after adding LevelID,
because the latter is the value passed to PSCI CPU_SUSPEND.

The arm64 implementations remain linked only for a built-in ACPI processor
driver. A module build therefore continues to use the existing weak-hook
behavior; repairing ARM64 modular LPI linkage is outside this change.

